WEBVTT

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.440
<i>We are now entering</i>
<i>the skies of the Second Ward.</i>

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.990
"The Octagon of Evil."

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.450
Have no fear.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.500
While it's true that many aircraft
go missing in this area,

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.910
the <i>Sky Whale II</i> is invincible.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.130
The <i>Sky Whale II </i>is
the world's most expensive

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.710
and most powerful armed helicopter,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.920
with a price of 5 billion esc.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.010
The surface of the aircraft is coated

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:47.300
with Magmell-sourced special material,
so please, put your mind at ease.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.220
We'll handle everything.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.350
I hope you're right.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.400
<i>There's a reason behind all the incidents.</i>

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.980
<i>If we solve the mystery</i>
<i>and obtain it for ourselves,</i>

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:01.940
<i>it will lead to massive</i>
<i>profits for Kyokusei.</i>

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:02.860
<i>But...</i>

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.860
<i>I didn't expect Miss Emilia to be here.</i>
<i>That was a miscalculation.</i>

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:43.530
What was that?

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:44.740
What in the world was that?

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.490
<i>We're being attacked from the ground.</i>

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:48.990
-What?
-What did you say?

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.990
<i>The subject can't be confirmed.</i>

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:54.910
Do something!

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.000
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:09.550
Excellent!

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:12.550
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:13.850
I've got nothing...

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.640
But, we've lost control.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:16.680
<i>What?</i>

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.560
<i>The engine's clear</i>
<i>and so are all the controls.</i>

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.440
<i>But somehow, we can't steer at all!</i>

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.360
What?

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:26.900
Have you gone mad?

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.030
<i>But, sir--!</i>

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.370
<i>We've lost control! We've lost control!</i>

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:38.750
Do something! I said, do something!

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:40.290
ERIN

00:04:58.390 --> 00:04:59.260
What's this?

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:00.970
Marshmallows.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.770
It's not quite time for dessert yet...

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.480
It's not dessert, it's lunch!

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:09.480
So what's for dessert?

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:10.730
Marshmallows.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:14.740
They were selling them in bulk
for cheap, so I stocked up!

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.780
That's why I'm having them as a main meal.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.660
You should probably return them.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.450
There's no such thing as
too many marshmallows.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:29.130
Well, I suppose it suits
your character, Zero...

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.130
Plus, we're poor.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.630
I had no choice but to buy them.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.010
Nice catch!

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.140
So, what's for dinner tonight?

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:42.930
Marshmallows.

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:44.850
Right.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:47.940
It's a client, sir!

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:50.730
How about breakfast...?

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:51.650
Sir!

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.030
So we meet again.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.860
I'm truly grateful for your services.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:02.830
So? What do you have for me today?

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:07.290
Yes... It's my daughter.
Emilia's gone missing in Magmell.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:10.670
So, it's the opposite of last time.
How troublesome.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.050
That area...

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:16.050
That's right.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:20.550
Emilia got lost in the area
called the Octagon of Evil.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:23.810
Please help me...

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:26.470
Mr. Inyo?

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.690
You went too far.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.520
She's not just lost, is she?

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:37.820
They were attacked by an unknown creature

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:40.360
and the <i>Sky Whale II</i> itself had
to execute an emergency landing.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.740
That's nothing new for Magmell.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:47.750
It all sounds right to me.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:49.080
Mr. Inyo...

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:52.580
Do you think there still are
unknown creatures in Magmell...?

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.590
My fees are double this time.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:55.800
What?

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:58.510
This happened because you all thought

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:02.260
and assumed you knew everything
there is to know about Magmell.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.060
You're very similar.

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:09.480
To Mr. Shuin.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.110
Well, there's nothing more to that.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.320
Talking to you made
me think of him, that's all.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.280
How is he doing, by the way?

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:27.620
Who knows.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:28.540
What?

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:29.450
Sir.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:30.620
Yes?

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:32.120
I changed my mind.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.210
My fees are triple this time.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.840
What? But...

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.670
How much more time are you going to waste?

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.090
Your daughter's lost in Magmell.

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:45.140
I understand. Let's proceed.

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:47.100
That's still not enough.

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:52.520
Hey, Zero. Quadrupling the fee is a bit--

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.900
Please eat them all before you leave.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.150
Yeah! Finish them! Or else.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.710
Miss, please stop.

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:18.130
It's dangerous out there.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:20.300
We can't just sit still.
We have to take action.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.380
I understand, but...

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.720
If they wanted to kill us,
they would've done so already.

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:28.140
They obviously have
something else in mind.

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:31.390
But, if something ever happens to you,
it'll be my responsibility--

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:32.930
Miss!

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:52.790
<i>People this far in the back regions?</i>

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:04.670
Zero, lead us and enter the area first.

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:05.930
Roger!

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.680
I suspect that it's them.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:09.890
You do?

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:11.680
Sir?

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:14.770
Please eat this when you get hungry.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.770
Actually, eat this even when you're not!

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.070
-No more, please...
-Okay, will do.

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:24.820
Miss! Miss Emilia!

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:27.740
Miss Emilia!

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:29.820
I'm glad you're back safe.

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.200
I've got great news.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:35.500
The rescue team is on
their way as we speak.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.960
Oh, don't look so concerned.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:42.380
Multiple units are on their way so there's
no way they'd be able to shoot us down.

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:57.270
Mr. Inyo!

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:01.440
It may be all over
by the time we get there.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:04.070
I just got word that
Kyokusei's paratroopers

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:05.940
are on their way to rescue them.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:08.610
Well, that's a shame.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:11.490
What? What... do you mean?

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.080
You'll see when we get there.

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:17.750
Here they come!

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:20.630
Kyokusei's best paratroopers!

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:45.730
We're wiped out...

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:47.150
This can't be!

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:54.950
Zero, how was it?

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:58.660
<i>Yes, as you expected, it's the Erin.</i>

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:01.710
Erin? What is that?

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:02.830
That.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.680
That's...

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:33.320
Get into attack position!

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:34.780
Mr. Owens?

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:37.290
It's the Erin... It has to be!

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:38.830
Erin?

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:41.710
They're the indigenous people of Magmell.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:44.210
Miss, stay put and don't get in the way.

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:51.220
Miss!

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:54.220
The indigenous people?

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:55.390
Yup.

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:57.310
Well...

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:01.180
We definitely could've
anticipated the situation, but...

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:06.190
Like I said, anything goes in Magmell.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.490
You knew it from the beginning, right?

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.610
Of course you did, you knew In.

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:19.370
<i>Sir!</i>

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:23.000
Sir, I've located the aircraft.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:25.750
It landed in the Erin's territory.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:32.470
Unfortunately,

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:34.720
the fertile-chested woman is alive.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:38.810
Your daughter's safe.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:40.680
Is that so?

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:42.230
What a relief.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:45.900
That's if she doesn't
provoke him any further.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:48.440
Owens!

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:52.740
No! You can't attack him.

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:55.660
It's not safe here. Please go back.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:58.160
-They just don't like weapons.
-It's here!

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.130
-Fire!
-No!

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:40.030
Retreat! We must retreat, Miss!

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:57.800
Sir, it's targeting you.

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:00.220
What? I wonder why.

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.510
Are you carrying a weapon by any chance?

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:04.270
Of course.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:05.890
In order to defend myself.

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:07.890
-Oh, brother.
<i>-Sir!</i>

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:11.730
-Let's go!
-What? Where?

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:12.770
Outside!

00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:23.160
-You better replace that helicopter.
-What?

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:46.390
<i>Their existence is barely known. But why?</i>

00:14:47.060 --> 00:14:51.060
<i>That's because a larger force</i>
<i>is covering them up.</i>

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:56.480
<i>But those who know</i>
<i>Magmell well are aware...</i>

00:14:57.110 --> 00:15:00.530
<i>Aware of their overwhelming</i>
<i>and terrifying powers.</i>

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:03.530
<i>The primitive tribe of Magmell...</i>

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:05.990
<i>The indigenous people: the Erin.</i>

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:10.790
<i>Nobody knows exactly who they are.</i>

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:14.670
<i>But humankind has already encountered</i>

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:17.760
<i>over 30 different species of them</i>
<i>in Magmell.</i>

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:24.010
<i>The Erin all possess innate abilities</i>
<i>that transcend normal humans.</i>

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:27.560
<i>Some can transform into giants,</i>

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:29.850
<i>some can walk in the sky,</i>

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:33.020
<i>some can throw lightning and emit poison.</i>

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.820
<i>While there are different types,</i>

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.730
<i>they all share two things in common.</i>

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:43.740
<i>One, they look relatively similar</i>
<i>to humans.</i>

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:49.000
<i>And two...</i>

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:53.500
<i>they possess an equal or higher</i>
<i>level of intelligence than humans.</i>

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.140
Hey!

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:08.260
Emilia!

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.980
-Daddy!
-Emilia.

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:16.060
Professor!

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:24.070
Daddy, it's not what it seems.
He's not at fault.

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.240
He just doesn't like weapons.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:27.450
I know.

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:29.660
Let's leave the rest to Mr. Inyo.

00:16:45.590 --> 00:16:46.430
Hey!

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:51.470
We've never met before, right?

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:56.440
Well, that's a new handshake.

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:58.900
Inyo!

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.070
You sure are fast.

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:12.620
I'd be a fool if I try to fight him.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:13.580
So...

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.290
Lachter.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:42.940
He looks like he's having fun.

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:45.740
-No, Inyo! You gotta stop!
-Emilia, it's okay.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:48.530
Lachter...

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:54.080
YO

00:18:18.230 --> 00:18:19.650
Checkmate!

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:22.650
Inyo!

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:58.930
Well, hey! Emilia, it's been a while.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:00.940
Inyo...

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:04.110
I appreciate you saving me,

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:07.690
but I don't think the Erin was an enemy.

00:19:08.530 --> 00:19:10.530
Yeah, I know.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:14.370
The Erin just don't like weapons.
So you didn't have to kill--

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:17.240
Yeah. So I didn't kill him.

00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:23.670
Excuse me... That's...

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:24.920
Yup!

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:27.210
Marshmallows!

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:28.420
What?

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:39.560
Delicious!

00:19:40.060 --> 00:19:41.850
I know, it's delicious!

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:43.310
But he doesn't think so!

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:06.250
They can't beat me!

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:16.350
I'm not an enemy either.
I hope you know that.

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:21.640
We all... just want... to live...

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:23.350
a peaceful life.

00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:27.690
Sorry to bother you.

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:29.900
I promise we'll never be back here again.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:36.370
He's Shuin's apprentice.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:38.910
Of course he knows how
to communicate with the Erin.

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:41.370
Professor! Miss!

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:44.210
I made a promise we'll never be back.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:47.540
If you break it, you'll be making me,
not just the Erin, your enemy as well.

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:49.750
What?

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:52.010
Mr. Inyo!

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:54.470
Since you saved us twice,

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:58.140
I'd like to gift you something
aside from the fee.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:00.430
Let's see...

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:04.980
How about a helicopter and something
besides marshmallows, perhaps?

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:08.150
Wait, what?

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:09.770
That's right!

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:12.940
The frogs know better than you, sir!

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:13.900
<i>What?</i>

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:19.910
I could do without
marshmallows for a while...

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:21.660
Right?

00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:11.810
PREVIEW

00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:14.440
<i>The old man silently cared for his gun.</i>

00:23:15.110 --> 00:23:17.030
<i>A worn-out bar,</i>

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:19.820
<i>tables with no customers...</i>

00:23:20.490 --> 00:23:24.450
<i>A white flower sways in the subtle wind.</i>

00:23:25.240 --> 00:23:28.950
<i>The old man silently cared for his gun.</i>

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:31.210
<i>A single petal</i>

00:23:31.290 --> 00:23:35.130
<i>floated in the sky</i>
<i>and landed on the ground.</i>

00:23:35.960 --> 00:23:40.010
<i>Next time, "Old Man and the Coffee Field."</i>
<i>Don't miss it.</i>

00:23:40.090 --> 00:23:41.090
Subtitle translation by Sachiko Takahashi
